# Android app configuration template (Secrets Gradle Plugin).
#
# The Secrets plugin is configured to read this file; on this branch it
# supplies NO BuildConfig fields (no provider secret of any kind).
#
# SECURITY NOTE (Phase 8.7-C / 8.7-C.1 / 8.7-C.3 / 8.7-D):
# Values compiled into the APK are recoverable from the distributed
# artifact and MUST NOT include reusable provider secrets.
# GEMINI_API_KEY has been REMOVED from the app:
#
#   * Android-distributed applications cannot keep a reusable provider
#     secret confidential.
#   * On this branch Android repository analysis is OFFLINE BY DEFAULT: the
#     app runs its deterministic, non-secret on-device template engine
#     (source badge OFFLINE_SIM).
#   * The authenticated server-side Gemini analysis path IS implemented on
#     this branch (Phase 8.7-D): the app sends a typed request with an
#     Authorization: Bearer <JWT> header to
#     POST /api/v1/repository/analyze; the gateway verifies the JWT and the
#     caller's role, and the agent-service calls Gemini using GEMINI_API_KEY
#     from its own server environment.
#   * The app holds no provider key — the settings field accepts only the
#     platform-issued gateway JWT. A failed live attempt is surfaced as
#     LIVE_FAILED and never becomes a fabricated "successful Gemini" result.
#   * The Gemini key belongs in the SERVER-SIDE environment of the
#     platform (devops-ai-platform / backend services), never in this file.
#
# No key in this file means the app runs its offline template engine (the
# default) or live analysis only when the operator has configured the
# gateway URL and JWT and the backend is configured server-side — never by
# falling back to a bundled credential.
